      "side": 1,
      "message": "include/private/base: Only dependencies on \u003csystem\u003e and other include/private/base files.\ninclude/private: Things like SkPathRef.h which are used by public APIs, but are not themselves public. These things will live in the core module (under srcs) or core_priv (under hdrs), with the former being preferred unless necessary. These *can* depend on include/core things.\n\nThe goal is include/private not to be empty, but to be much smaller.\n\nThe next step *is* to move more files from include/private to include/private/base (based on the findings from https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/616777).",
      "parentUuid": "a495bc28_ed9d3e23",
